                <pb facs="0142" n="132" sameAs="frus:frus1941v06/pg132"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (3)/100: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >White</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-12-24T23:00:00-05:00">December 24, 1941—11
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>330. Your 276, December 23, noon. This Government has informed the Dominican
                    Government that it perceives no objection to the introduction by the Dominican
                    Government on its own responsibility of a resolution calling for a declaration
                    of war on the part of all the American Republics.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
